## 14. Validation — Everyone's Responsibility (not a separate module)

Each module validates its own inputs directly inside its own `add`/`update` methods.
Minimum required checks, per the project description:

- IDs must be unique and valid
- Quantities must be greater than zero
- Prices must be greater than or equal to zero
- Phone numbers must follow a valid format
- Required fields (like name) must not be empty
- Dates and times must be valid and logical

---

## 15. Main Menu & Integration — Owner: Kareem

The final program has one `main()` (everyone else's test `main()` gets removed when
their file is combined). The main menu matches the required options:

1. Employee Management
2. Kitchen Management
3. Payment Management
4. Delivery Management
5. Reports
6. Search
7. Validation
0. Exit

`RestaurantSystem` — the class that owns one instance of every manager above
(`CustomerManager`, `TableManager`, `MenuManager`, `ReservationManager`,
`OrderManager`, `EmployeeManager`, `KitchenManager`, `PaymentManager`,
`DeliveryManager`, `ReportManager`) and runs this menu loop. Only this class is
allowed to make different managers work together.
